course: dictionary
lesson: 8192
title: Restless: feelings and moving things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Restless describes someone who cannot keep still or relax. You might feel restless on a long car trip because you are bored, worried or full of energy. «Back in the kitchen the Rat is restless, overcoat on and pistols in his belt, worried the river will run off without him.» The Rat cannot settle because he is worried, so restless means unable to keep still.
explain: Restless can also describe a night. «A restless night» is a night with little or bad sleep, when you toss and turn. Check the meaning by swapping it in: "I had a restless night" becomes "I did not sleep well", and that still makes sense.
explain: Restless can describe things that keep moving, not only people. «The restless sea» is the sea that never stays still, and «a restless dripping mill-wheel» keeps turning. Restless is an adjective, so it describes a noun.
fact: Restless means unable to keep still or relax.
fact: People feel restless when they are bored, worried or full of energy.
fact: A restless night is a night with little or bad sleep.
fact: «The restless sea» means the sea that keeps moving.
fact: «A restless revolving squirrel» is a squirrel that keeps moving in a turning cage.
fact: Restless is an adjective, and its comparative form is more restless.
exercise: «The children sat restless through the long assembly.» What does restless mean here? | *Unable to keep still | Very happy and calm | Hungry for lunch | Fast asleep
exercise: «Ali had a restless night and woke up tired.» What does a restless night mean? | A night full of stars | A night spent dancing | A night in a tent | *A night with little or bad sleep
exercise: «The restless sea rolled in and out all day.» What does restless describe? | The day, which was very long | The sun, which was hot | The sand, which was dry | *The sea, which never stays still
test: Boredom is «the restless feeling of having nothing to do». What does restless suggest about boredom? | A feeling of nothing at all | A calm, sleepy feeling | *A feeling of being unable to keep still | A feeling of being completely sure
test: Which form is the comparative of restless? | restlessly | restlesser | restlessest | *more restless
exam: The Rat lies by the dusty lane, «restless», dreaming of seas and ships. Why is the Rat restless? | He has eaten too much food | He is cold and wet from the rain | *He longs to see the world beyond the hills | He is fast asleep and snoring
